   "notes": [
    "Actual general-fund results for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025, as reported to the MA Division of Local Services on Schedule A, not a budget.",
    "Includes public schools. Massachusetts cities and towns pay for their schools and their share of any regional school district through the town budget, where most other states have separate school districts, so spending and property tax per resident run higher than in those states.",
    "Covers the general fund. Water, sewer and other enterprise funds, and fire, water and other districts inside the town, are separate and not included.",
    "Debt is all long-term debt the town reported outstanding at the end of FY 2025 (Schedule A Part 10), including school construction and any water, sewer or other enterprise fund borrowing.",
    "\"Taxes\" on Schedule A include motor vehicle and other local excises ($19,874,745), which are shown as other local taxes. The rest, with penalties and interest, is shown as property tax.",
    "Left out: transfers in from the town's own funds ($1,641,715) and other financing sources such as bond proceeds ($582,300), which are not new revenue.",
    "Fixed costs ($28,693,638: health insurance, pensions and other benefits for town and school staff) are spread across departments in proportion to their size, schools included, as with benefits in other states. Debt service is left out of that spread.",
    "Intergovernmental assessments and other spending ($1,562,695: charter school tuition, regional transit and county and state charges) are spread across departments in proportion to their size.",
    "Political money counts contributions from unions and registered PACs to Nantucket's party ward, town and city committees, filed with the Office of Campaign and Political Finance since 2023. Corporate contributions are banned in Massachusetts. Individuals and money passed between candidate and party committees are not counted. Candidates for town office file with the town clerk, so their own committees are not included, and party committees also support state candidates.",
    "Transparency practices have not been checked yet, so they are not scored."
